Start with a running server from the [LLMD quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart')).
The example below uses Python 3 and its standard library.

# [Connect an application]($heading.id('connect-an-application'))

Set the base URL to your server's address with the `/v1` suffix. Read the
model ID from the server so the client also works when the operator sets a
custom model name.

```python
import json
from urllib.request import Request, urlopen

base_url = "http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1"
with urlopen(f"{base_url}/models") as response:
    model_id = json.load(response)["data"][0]["id"]

payload = {
    "model": model_id,
    "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reply with a short greeting."}],
}
request = Request(
    f"{base_url}/chat/completions",
    data=json.dumps(payload).encode(),
    headers={"Content-Type": "application/json"},
)
with urlopen(request) as response:
    print(json.load(response)["choices"][0]["message"]["content"])
```

For a deployment that requires authentication, supply its credentials on both
requests. See the [chat completion reference]($link.page('llmd/api').ref('create-a-chat-completion'))
for response fields and generation settings.

# [Stream a chat completion]($heading.id('stream-a-chat-completion'))

Set `stream` to `true` to receive server-sent events. Read events as they
arrive and append each `choices[0].delta.content` value when present.
An optional usage event has an empty `choices` array. Stop at `[DONE]`.
The [streaming request example]($link.page('llmd/api').ref('stream-a-chat-completion'))
shows how to inspect the event stream with curl.

# [Call tools from a client]($heading.id('call-tools-from-a-client'))

Use a checkpoint and chat template that support tool calls. Pass function
definitions in `tools`. When the assistant returns a tool call, validate its
name and arguments, run the function in the client, and send the result in a
new completion. Include the original assistant message and a `tool` message
with the matching `tool_call_id`. The [tool call reference]($link.page('llmd/api').ref('call-tools-from-a-client'))
includes a function schema and the expected message fields.
